    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's helpful. So if I'm following you, the liberal side seems to be building their case on modern concepts of human rights and personal autonomy, whereas the conservative side's arguments seem more heavily dependent on traditional dogma and the idea of suffering being part of a \"plan.\" Do you think the liberal framework is more philosophically robust in a contemporary secular society, or is it just a different type of theological interpretation?",
